<blockquote class="uncited"><div>I did the suggested modifications but the application hangs up in the middle of the first demo.</div></blockquote>The suggested modification affects only the LAST demo... and I've compiled and run the demo without problems... <img class="smilies" src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/images/smilies/icon_smile.gif" width="15" height="15" alt=":)" title="Smile"> <br><br>The other issue you're having refers to the default Bullet ConvexDecomposition demo and not to the topic discussed in this series of posts (and I'm not very familiar with that demo).<br>Anyway usually there are some parameters you can tune to adjust the convex decomposition result.<br><br>P.S. Please note that you can still use "btHACDCompoundShape.h" alone (without the whole HACDDemo) to add HACD support to ANY Bullet program (but you need to compile the HACD SVN library beforehand).<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2180">Flix</a> — Thu May 09, 2013 9:17 am</p><hr />
